      "body": "## Purpose\n\nThe documented fallback for concurrent users is max_concurrent_requests, but request_rate takes precedence when the configured user-count key is absent. Dividing tokens/s by requests/s produces tokens/request and can turn an unlimited request rate into zero per-user throughput. Use the documented concurrency fallback.\n\nThis only changes runs where the key named by `--user-count-var` is missing from the record. Ordinary `bench serve` output writes `max_concurrency` (as `None` when unset), which already fell through to `max_concurrent_requests`. That measured value is overcounted at second boundaries until #56653 is fixed, so fallback runs can still read low.\n\nOpen PRs #55607/#55658 fix frontier dominance and #56111 fixes GPU-count discovery. This changes only user-count inference; no competing fix was found.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n`.venv/bin/python -m pytest --noconftest tests/benchmarks/sweep/test_pareto_metrics.py tests/benchmarks/test_plot_filters.py -q`\n\nCPU benchmark-postprocessing tests import the repository modules directly. The global GPU-engine conftest is excluded for this focused run. Model execution was not changed or evaluated.\n\n## Test Result\n\nFour regressions fail before. The five new input-metric tests and 27 existing plot-filter tests pass after (32 total). Changed-file pre-commit and Python 3.12 mypy pass.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
